# ded-exit.conf -- dedicated-IP egress layer control (survives redeploys,
# same mechanism as mode.conf / dedicated.conf). Read by the
# surflare-proxy wrapper on every proxy start.
#
# EXIT_VIA_DED=1  all proxied flows chain through the dedicated SOCKS
#                 exit.  Arrival path is the DED_VIA knob below.
# EXIT_VIA_DED=0  layer disabled.
#                 The wrapper's jq filter output is byte-identical
#                 to the pre-ded-exit filter (verified by md5 in
#                 tests/ded-exit-inject.sh), i.e. plain relay.
#
# DED_SERVER/PORT/USER/PASS: the dedicated SOCKS endpoint sold by the
# provider app.  Port must be numeric; incomplete or malformed config
# disables the layer and logs to syslog (tag surflare-proxy) -- fail
# safe to plain relay.
#
# Credential rotation: unknown cadence.  The canary
# (surflare-ded-canary) detects a revoked credential on the next 1-minute probe tick
# and flips EXIT_VIA_DED to 0; the daily re-attach probe flips it back
# only after a shadow-instance probe succeeds.
#
# NOTE: this template contains NO credentials.  Deploy as
# /etc/surflare/ded-exit.conf on the router with the real values from
# the provider app (SOCKS5 Proxy card).  The real file must never be
# committed to this repository.
# DEPLOY: replace every <...> placeholder below with the real value
# from the provider app before copying to the router.  Leftover
# placeholders are rejected by the validator and the layer stays off.
#
# Values are taken verbatim to the end of the line -- no inline
# comments after a value (the parser does not strip them and the
# validator would reject the whole layer); put comments on their own
# line.  A password may contain # safely when quoted normally.
# Keys must start at column 0 -- a leading space or tab makes the
# parser silently skip the line.
EXIT_VIA_DED="0"
DED_SERVER="<SOCKS server from provider app>"
DED_PORT="<SOCKS port from provider app>"
DED_USER="<SOCKS username from provider app>"
DED_PASS="<SOCKS password from provider app>"
# DED_VIA selects how the socks outbound reaches the dedicated server:
#   direct  dial it over the WAN (no carrier detour).  After the
#           2026-10-18 power cycle the provider stopped honoring
#           relay-arrival bindings -- carrier-detoured connections were
#           refused with socks code=5 while direct arrivals kept the
#           dedicated egress (evidence: logs 2026-10-18 20:42-21:47).
#   carrier (or unset) historical behavior: detour through the carrier
#           urltest group.
DED_VIA="direct"
